{
 "readings": {
  "E1": "calendar = D17's dates (the EXTENDED published NAVs) of the book from its first date to END; END = the last row of the three D03 Master files (2026-10-30), not D17's last date; rows after END are dropped on read and never used; D18 prices on other dates are never read",
  "E2": "decision dates = T0 and the last D17 session of every later ISO week; the decision at the last session is not traded",
  "E3": "label = latest Master row dated <= decision date, per index and for MAUc1 (D24); IN iff all three index SIGN are BUY; g = BUY iff the MAUc1 SIGN is BUY (a week whose row is dated after its last D17 session reads the previous week's row)",
  "E4": "initial position at T0 close, no cost: OUT = gw GOLDBEES and (1-gw) cash of NAV 1 with gw = 0.8 (g BUY at T0) or 0.2 (SELL), 0.5 in fixed50 mode; IN = the basket in force at T0 as drifted since its availableDate (OHLC4 of the first D18 session on or after it), scaled to NAV 1",
  "E5": "a basket takes effect on the first calendar session on or after its availableDate; baskets flagged csv_only_skipped are dropped; weights are renormalised to 1",
  "E6": "stock fill = OHLC4 of the Eikon bar (close if any of open/high/low is blank; last close if the stock has no bar that session)",
  "E7": "costs: one rule for every trade, see the module docstring (cost on the value traded, targets scaled by (V-cost)/V)",
  "E8": "a basket change while IN trades from the old holdings to the new basket (delta trades); while OUT nothing is traded; a flip of g while IN is not a trade",
  "E9": "a switch and a basket change on the same session: the switch trades into / out of the basket in force that session",
  "E10": "cash level: the extended LBES (D11) as-of on sessions; it covers the window and the engine asserts that no session of any window lies after the file's last date (0 accrued sessions)",
  "E11": "constant mix: stock share f = invested decision weeks / decision weeks, rebalanced at every decision date's next session (T0 included) and at every basket change; constant_mix splits the non-stock share 50/50, constant_mix_timed by the decision's gw; initial stock holding = drifted basket scaled by f",
  "E13": "R3 live window starts at the first D17 session on or after 2021-11-01 with its own spells and totals (in-or-out and gold), own draws (same seeds), the SAME bounds (the book's full-window HI_in, HI_out, HI_buy, HI_sell) and free initial position in the state decided then",
  "E14": "R2 cash = LBES to the session before 2024-01-24, then chained with the desk's LIQUIDCASE returns on sessions (liquidEtfFinal_extended)",
  "E15": "V4(d) always-in runs on the whole window (to END = 2026-10-30); G0 = +-0.25 pp/yr overall and +-0.5 pp every calendar year",
  "E16": "GOLDBEES fill: T03's de-spike (OHLC4 of open/high/low clipped to MCX gold's range that day + 0.5%) on every session up to the MCX file's last date (2026-09-28); on later sessions the raw OHLC4 of the Eikon bar, no clipping, no scaling, no tolerance band",
  "T06-1": "sessions_invested = number of daily returns t = 1..T-1 earned while the parent is held (state j is held from its trade session dec_idx[j]+1; T0 for j = 0)",
  "T06-4": "the sampler draws one uniform per part, including the last part (whose length is forced), so a draw consumes k uniforms; cumulative probabilities are exact integer prefix sums divided by the exact total, searchsorted side='right' (T06's functions, unchanged; the gold draws call them with the gold seed and the gold (k, S, bounds))",
  "T06-5": "V5(c): the sum of the lengths of a draw is fixed, so the check is made per spell position: the mean of its length over the draws within 4 standard errors of S/k (in-or-out and gold)",
  "T06-7": "window-coverage check: the through-date of every approved file the run reads must reach END, except D12 (the de-spike range, raw OHLC4 after it), the basket files D19/D05 (through the newest basket) and the OLD D17 files (pinned, read only for V4(e)); D17/D24 files are read only up to END",
  "T06-8": "the 'weeks' of draw_states.npz and of every V3/V5 statement are the weekly decision rows (410 for SCMO_0003/0010/0029, 409 for SCMO_0007 on the full window)",
  "T08-1": "gold bounds: lo = LO = 2 (= the shortest actual gold spell), hi_buy and hi_sell = the longest BUY and SELL spell of each book's own full-window gold series, asserted to be 68 and 28 (the in-or-out bounds are asserted to be 46 and 40); the live window uses the same bounds",
  "T08-2": "trade log columns: gw_after = the sleeve's gold weight target after the trade (0.8 / 0.2 / 0.5) on every row of every run except hold_parent, where it is empty; on a switch_in row it is the gold weight of that decision (irrelevant to the position, which holds no sleeve)",
  "T08-3": "V4: T06's last decision (2026-10-22, a Thursday, the last session of its calendar) is compared with T08's decision of 2026-10-23 (the same week); T08's j-th decision equals T06's for j <= 408 and T06's draw states get T08's real state of the extra last week appended (the decision of 2026-10-30, not traded)",
  "T08-4": "the number of sleeve trades of a draw (draws.csv sleeve_trades) is counted from the states: decisions j >= 1 with a trade session inside the window, OUT at j-1 and j, and g[j] != g[j-1]; it is 0 in fixed50 mode. The engine checks this count against the recorded trades of the real rule (V6)",
  "T08-5": "V4(c): T06's draw curves are float32, so they are compared after casting the replayed NAV to float32 (relative tolerance 1e-6); T06's states are 409 weeks, replayed with T08's decision of that week (2026-10-23), the NAV compared on the sessions up to 2026-10-22"
 },
